  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "How to run",
      "items": [
        "cargo run --release --bin states_traj -- --state minus-x|neel|neel-x --L 16 --gammas 0,0.01,0.1 --trajectories 112 [--unravel diffusive|jump] [--traj-seed N] [--channel z|x|y|dep] [--ent-dt Δ] [--stop-te F]",
        "Writes to data/ (or $SCARS_DATA_DIR); the scripts read data/used_data/ (lean runs in its lean/ folder)",
        "Analysis order: fit_states.py → fit_small_gamma.py → fit_states_inverse_L.py (Γ_∞ from states_rates.csv) → single_kick.py; fit_channels.py → spreading.py; plot_states.py any time"
      ] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Key mechanics",
      "items": [
        "Diffusive (default): e^(−iH dt/2) · random rotations e^(−iθσ^α_j), θ ~ N(0, rate·γ dt) · e^(−iH dt/2); channels z, x, y, dep",
        "Jump (σᶻ only): σᶻ_j kicks at total rate γL, site uniform, exact e^(−iHτ) between; the scar start stays analytic until the first kick",
        "All trajectories advance together; every CSV row is the mean and standard error, flushed at once (a cut job keeps its early part)",
        "Stop: signal below max(--stop, 3σ) for 10 time units, or at --stop-te × first 1/e time; step min(dt, 0.05/γ)"
      ] },
    { "dot": "violet", "title": "Notes part",
      "items": [
        "Compile: latex/build_parts.sh trajectories → latex/parts/pdf/trajectories.pdf (full notes are built first; numbering as in latex/notes.tex)",
        "§1 Model; §2.4 Other single-site noise channels",
        "§3.1–3.3 Notation, Pauli strings, Pure states: trajectories and single flips",
        "§3.6 Entanglement entropy; §3.8 Other single-site noise channels; §3.10 Entanglement along trajectories and after a single flip; §3.11 Eigenvalues without LAPACK; §3.12 Run options and file names",
        "§4 How the decay rates are computed",
        "§6 Scar against thermal decay up to L = 20; §7 Small γ: the finite-size cap",
        "§10.1 Runs and checks; §10.2 Thermodynamic rates under every noise channel"
      ] }
  ]
